{"matches":[{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"High","urls":["https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/security/advisories/GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-111181","https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/commit/1260c3845f54502a05a87594f09a334786bb34d7","https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/commit/f7075eae3a84c3473ab4bf0a777da28db208e916","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/releases/tag/1.20.9","https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/releases/tag/v2.4.0"],"description":"body-parser vulnerable to Denial of Service via trailing bytes after a compressed request body","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-111181","epss":0.00388,"percentile":0.33649,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-111181","cwe":"CWE-248","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["2.4.0"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"2.4.0","date":"2026-10-24","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.29100000000000004},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-111181","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-111181","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"High","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/security/advisories/GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828"],"description":"body-parser is body parsing middleware for Node.js and Express. In versions before 1.20.9 and in versions from 2.0.0 before 2.4.0, a single request can crash any application using body-parser with default options. When a request carries a Content-Encoding such as gzip, body-parser pipes it into a decompression stream and, after reading the body, leaves that stream with no error listener. A payload of one valid compressed frame followed by trailing bytes decodes and the application responds normally, but the trailing bytes then reach the already-finished decoder, which emits an error that is re-thrown as an uncaught exception and terminates the process. No matching route is required because body parsing runs before routing, so any endpoint that parses a body is affected. The issue is fixed in body-parser 2.4.0 and 1.20.9, and users should upgrade to one of those versions or later. As a workaround, disable request-body inflation (set the body-parser inflate option to false) so encoded requests are rejected before any decompression stream is created.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-111181","epss":0.00388,"percentile":0.33649,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-111181","cwe":"CWE-248","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"body-parser","version":"2.3.0"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828","versionConstraint":">=2.0.0,<2.4.0 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"2.4.0"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/body-parser@2.3.0","name":"body-parser","version":"2.3.0","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/body-parser@2.3.0","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-qv5m-9pm6-hqp3","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qv5m-9pm6-hqp3","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/node-server/security/advisories/GHSA-qv5m-9pm6-hqp3","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/commit/61cc0267e613e684401f17c27538ba3bf97339a4","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/releases/tag/v2.1.6"],"description":"@hono/node-server: Unhandled `ECONNRESET` on the socket during an asynchronous WebSocket upgrade crashes the process","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126343","epss":0.00453,"percentile":0.40144,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126343","cwe":"CWE-248","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["2.1.6"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"2.1.6","date":"2026-11-13","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.23329500000000003},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-126343","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-126343","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/node-server/commit/61cc0267e613e684401f17c27538ba3bf97339a4","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/releases/tag/v2.1.6","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/security/advisories/GHSA-qv5m-9pm6-hqp3"],"description":"@hono/node-server allows running the Hono application on Node.js. From 2.0.0 until 2.1.6, the WebSocket upgrade handler waits for the Hono application to finish asynchronous middleware or handler work without first attaching an error listener to the socket. If an unauthenticated client resets the TCP connection during that window, the socket emits an unhandled ECONNRESET error and terminates the Node.js process. If a global uncaughtException handler suppresses termination, the pending upgrade waiter is not released and repeated requests can grow the heap. This affects applications that enable WebSocket support and perform asynchronous work on the upgrade path. This issue is fixed in version 2.1.6.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126343","epss":0.00453,"percentile":0.40144,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126343","cwe":"CWE-248","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"@hono/node-server","version":"2.1.5"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-qv5m-9pm6-hqp3","versionConstraint":">=2.0.0,<2.1.6 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"2.1.6"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/@hono/node-server@2.1.5","name":"@hono/node-server","version":"2.1.5","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/%40hono/node-server@2.1.5","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-4m76-xfj5-7975","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4m76-xfj5-7975","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-4m76-xfj5-7975","https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/34f90432a1794b28e52802670efcd01963f716d6","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16"],"description":"Hono: `mount()` and `app.mount()` can forward a path that bypasses middleware scoped inside the mount prefix","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126357","epss":0.004,"percentile":0.3497,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126357","cwe":"CWE-288","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["4.13.16"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"4.13.16","date":"2026-11-13","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.20600000000000002},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-126357","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-126357","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/34f90432a1794b28e52802670efcd01963f716d6","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16","https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-4m76-xfj5-7975"],"description":"Hono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. Prior to 4.13.16, mount() and app.mount() can remove a dynamic mount prefix using the route-pattern length rather than the matched-prefix length, allowing a crafted path to be forwarded as a protected inner route while the outer application routes the original path. Since 4.12.21, rebuilding the forwarded URL from the decoded pathname can also convert a decoded backslash to a slash and collapse parent-directory segments, again causing the mounted application to receive a protected path. An unauthenticated client can use either applicable path transformation to reach a mounted route without authentication or authorization middleware scoped to a subpath inside the mount prefix. This issue is fixed in version 4.13.16.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126357","epss":0.004,"percentile":0.3497,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126357","cwe":"CWE-288","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"hono","version":"4.13.13"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-4m76-xfj5-7975","versionConstraint":"<4.13.16 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"4.13.16"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","name":"hono","version":"4.13.13","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-4h7h-rv7c-7m2v","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4h7h-rv7c-7m2v","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-4h7h-rv7c-7m2v","https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/d88fab372415277a9e540e895650943dd08eef4a","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16"],"description":"Hono: `validator('form')` skips validation for `multipart/form-data` requests with extra parameters","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126356","epss":0.00392,"percentile":0.34107,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126356","cwe":"CWE-20","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["4.13.16"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"4.13.16","date":"2026-11-13","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.20187999999999998},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-126356","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-126356","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/d88fab372415277a9e540e895650943dd08eef4a","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16","https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-4h7h-rv7c-7m2v"],"description":"Hono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. From 4.5.1 until 4.13.16, validator('form') uses a strict whole-header pattern that fails to recognize multipart/form-data when its Content-Type includes another legal parameter or extra whitespace after a semicolon. The validation callback receives an empty object even though c.req.parseBody() or c.req.formData() can still parse and expose all submitted fields to the handler. An unauthenticated client can therefore bypass allow-list or required-field checks when the application relies on the form validator and its callback accepts an empty object. application/x-www-form-urlencoded requests are not affected. This issue is fixed in version 4.13.16.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126356","epss":0.00392,"percentile":0.34107,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126356","cwe":"CWE-20","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"hono","version":"4.13.13"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-4h7h-rv7c-7m2v","versionConstraint":">=4.5.1,<=4.13.15 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"4.13.16"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","name":"hono","version":"4.13.13","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-jpvv-r467-5p4w","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jpvv-r467-5p4w","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/node-server/security/advisories/GHSA-jpvv-r467-5p4w","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/commit/3868998a805ae79216535ad3986c1e7228dee313","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/commit/fb97395ec36af66567c76976e741110b02804d1c","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/releases/tag/v1.19.18","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/releases/tag/v2.1.6"],"description":"@hono/node-server: Backslash in the request path is parsed as a path separator, bypassing path-based access control at a reverse proxy","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126210","epss":0.00375,"percentile":0.32163,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126210","cwe":"CWE-436","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["2.1.6"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"2.1.6","date":"2026-11-13","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.193125},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-126210","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-126210","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/node-server/commit/3868998a805ae79216535ad3986c1e7228dee313","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/commit/fb97395ec36af66567c76976e741110b02804d1c","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/releases/tag/v1.19.18","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/releases/tag/v2.1.6","https://github.com/honojs/node-server/security/advisories/GHSA-jpvv-r467-5p4w"],"description":"@hono/node-server allows running the Hono application on Node.js. Prior to 1.19.18 and from 2.0.0 until 2.1.6, the server passes a raw request-target containing a backslash in its path to the WHATWG URL parser, which treats the backslash as a path separator and resolves dot segments. A reverse proxy, load balancer, or web application firewall that preserves the backslash and applies path-based rules to the original request can therefore permit a request that the application normalizes to a blocked route. This lets an unauthenticated client reach route content that the upstream component was intended to deny, while Hono application access controls are unaffected because they operate on the normalized path. This issue is fixed in versions 1.19.18 and 2.1.6.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126210","epss":0.00375,"percentile":0.32163,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126210","cwe":"CWE-436","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"@hono/node-server","version":"2.1.5"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-jpvv-r467-5p4w","versionConstraint":">=2.0.0,<2.1.6 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"2.1.6"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/@hono/node-server@2.1.5","name":"@hono/node-server","version":"2.1.5","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/%40hono/node-server@2.1.5","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-h7mg-cq63-vhpq","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-h7mg-cq63-vhpq","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-h7mg-cq63-vhpq","https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/8a103aa59bcfbffd5396b1548a0dff3688777c36","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16"],"description":"Hono: RegExpRouter skips wildcard middleware for some route sets and for paths with an encoded line terminator","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126358","epss":0.00367,"percentile":0.31228,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126358","cwe":"CWE-863","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["4.13.16"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"4.13.16","date":"2026-11-13","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.189005},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-126358","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-126358","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/8a103aa59bcfbffd5396b1548a0dff3688777c36","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16","https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-h7mg-cq63-vhpq"],"description":"Hono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. From 4.1.4 until 4.13.16, RegExpRouter can omit wildcard middleware in three version-specific cases: since 4.13.0, middleware using the explicit default parameter pattern in /api/:tenant{[^/]+}/admin/* is not applied to a route written as /api/:tenant/admin/:id; since 4.1.4, middleware on /admin/* is not applied to a route registered as /admin* for paths under /admin/; and since 4.4.0, a request path containing an encoded line terminator can reach the not-found handler without wildcard middleware. The default SmartRouter selects RegExpRouter for most applications, and the router's registration-time coverage calculation treated the first two matching pattern pairs as different while its compiled wildcard did not match line terminators in the third case. An unauthenticated client can reach a route handler or the not-found handler without authentication or authorization middleware registered on the wildcard path. TrieRouter, LinearRouter, and PatternRouter apply the middleware in the three described cases. This issue is fixed in version 4.13.16.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":3.9,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126358","epss":0.00367,"percentile":0.31228,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126358","cwe":"CWE-863","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"hono","version":"4.13.13"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-h7mg-cq63-vhpq","versionConstraint":">=4.1.4,<=4.13.15 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"4.13.16"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","name":"hono","version":"4.13.13","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110306","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/39933a1f1422986f14e2d844f552238feb40f5d4","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/597f254c86d151568511eeb9a1df761fd12520b3","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/e60e716f41d1d73717e2d803d20b68d2c6d20a0f","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.8","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.9","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.2.3"],"description":"fast-uri vulnerable to URI scheme spoofing via percent-encoded scheme decoding","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":6.1,"exploitabilityScore":2.9,"impactScore":2.8},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110306","epss":0.0025,"percentile":0.16425,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110306","cwe":"CWE-172","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-110306","cwe":"CWE-180","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["3.1.9"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"3.1.9","date":"2026-10-24","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.13874999999999998},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-110306","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110306","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg"],"description":"fast-uri is a dependency-free RFC 3986 URI parser and serializer for Node.js. In versions before 2.4.8, from 3.0.0 through 3.1.8, and from 4.0.0 through 4.2.2, fast-uri percent-decodes the scheme component with the legacy global unescape() function before validating it, so an input whose decoded scheme is a dangerous token is emitted as a live scheme even though RFC 3986 does not allow percent-encoding in a scheme and no other parser accepts it. An application that screens dangerous schemes on the raw input and then stores or renders the normalized or resolved result can turn an inert string into an executable javascript, data, or vbscript URL, producing a stored or reflected cross-site scripting vector, and the equal() comparison treats an encoded and a plain scheme as the same, which can bypass equality-based allowlists. The issue is fixed in fast-uri 2.4.8, 3.1.9, and 4.2.3, and users should upgrade to one of these versions or later. As a workaround, reject input whose scheme part contains a percent sign, or check the parsed scheme against an allowlist after normalization and use that same parsed result rather than the raw string.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":6.1,"exploitabilityScore":2.9,"impactScore":2.8},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110306","epss":0.0025,"percentile":0.16425,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110306","cwe":"CWE-172","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-110306","cwe":"CWE-180","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"fast-uri","version":"3.1.8"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg","versionConstraint":">=3.0.0,<3.1.9 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"3.1.9"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/fast-uri@3.1.8","name":"fast-uri","version":"3.1.8","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["BSD-3-Clause"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/fast-uri@3.1.8","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-wjr9-j795-jxcr","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-wjr9-j795-jxcr","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-wjr9-j795-jxcr","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110180","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/58c183d0b168ad87f98773266444ce1f6375803a","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/ddfc6a51122dfce0365655f04479fc3adb7f6b3c","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/f6d46dfeab025d0c440485f4ae29fa4f14707646","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.8","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.9","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.2.3"],"description":"fast-uri vulnerable to host confusion via unchecked WHATWG host canonicalization","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":4.8,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":2.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110180","epss":0.00255,"percentile":0.1721,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110180","cwe":"CWE-20","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-110180","cwe":"CWE-436","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["3.1.9"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"3.1.9","date":"2026-10-24","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.12494999999999999},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-110180","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110180","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-wjr9-j795-jxcr"],"description":"fast-uri is a dependency-free RFC 3986 URI parser and serializer for Node.js. In versions from 2.4.2 through 2.4.7, from 3.1.3 through 3.1.8, and from 4.0.1 through 4.2.2, for HTTP-family schemes the canonicalizeHost() function passes the parsed host to the WHATWG URL parser and adopts its hostname without checking that the parser consumed the entire input as a host, so the authority can be silently rewritten: data before an at-sign is dropped and tab, carriage-return, and line-feed characters are stripped, with no error reported. An application that enforces host-based policy such as denylists, loopback filtering, redirect validation, or outbound proxy routing on one representation can then see the canonical host diverge from what it checked, allowing traffic to be steered to an unintended destination. The issue is fixed in fast-uri 2.4.8, 3.1.9, and 4.2.3, and users should upgrade to one of these versions or later. As a workaround, reject an authority that contains more than one at-sign or any tab, carriage-return, or line-feed before calling fast-uri, or treat any non-empty parse error as fatal and compare hosts only from the same parse result.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":4.8,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":2.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110180","epss":0.00255,"percentile":0.1721,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110180","cwe":"CWE-20","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-110180","cwe":"CWE-436","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"fast-uri","version":"3.1.8"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-wjr9-j795-jxcr","versionConstraint":">=3.1.3,<3.1.9 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"3.1.9"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/fast-uri@3.1.8","name":"fast-uri","version":"3.1.8","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["BSD-3-Clause"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/fast-uri@3.1.8","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Low","urls":["https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110725","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/39e6493c1356f30a0084171627eb266786e1620e","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/a9b8d67353630aab053cd727cf629023dd018d2b","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.8","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.9","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.2.3"],"description":"fast-uri vulnerable to scheme injection via an unescaped first-segment colon in suffix references","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":3.7,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110725","epss":0.00302,"percentile":0.23347,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110725","cwe":"CWE-41","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-110725","cwe":"CWE-116","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["3.1.9"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"3.1.9","date":"2026-10-24","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.10117},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-110725","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110725","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Low","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp"],"description":"fast-uri is a dependency-free RFC 3986 URI parser and serializer for Node.js. In versions before 2.4.8, from 3.0.0 through 3.1.8, and from 4.0.0 through 4.2.2, when serialize(), normalize(), or resolve() are called with the non-default option reference set to suffix on a reference that has no authority, the emitted relative reference can contain a bare colon in its first path segment without escaping it, even though RFC 3986 forbids that because it makes the string reparse as an absolute URI with a scheme. An application that serializes or normalizes a relative reference with the suffix option and then treats the result as a URI can turn inert input into a live javascript, data, or vbscript URL, a cross-site scripting vector, and the equal() comparison can conflate a scheme-bearing reference with a relative one. Exposure is limited to applications using the non-default suffix reference option. The issue is fixed in fast-uri 2.4.8, 3.1.9, and 4.2.3, and users should upgrade to one of these versions or later. As a workaround, avoid the suffix reference option on untrusted input, or percent-encode a colon in the first path segment of the result before treating it as a URI.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":3.7,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110725","epss":0.00302,"percentile":0.23347,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110725","cwe":"CWE-41","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-110725","cwe":"CWE-116","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"fast-uri","version":"3.1.8"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-333x-w4r6-6crp","versionConstraint":">=3.0.0,<3.1.9 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"3.1.9"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/fast-uri@3.1.8","name":"fast-uri","version":"3.1.8","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["BSD-3-Clause"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/fast-uri@3.1.8","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Low","urls":["https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110095","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/048bbd0a252971be86d6579f0dfc87f8de5b9c47","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/52774a5c35df36b0bbe439cd4c12c3dc0e50e3b9","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/7c19f8b97ec51f1f20b4e3d9d5820cb8d5176058","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/9eb8759a9825c046f57f7f695f1944bc39b88abd","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/acc5c5d60c4209571789496e1732468911c7e12a","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/b110a3571c37dfcf9d1c72ce2e2e178c78d1a424","https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.8","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.9","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.2.3"],"description":"fast-uri vulnerable to improper path equivalence in relative reference normalization","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":3.7,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110095","epss":0.00289,"percentile":0.21831,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110095","cwe":"CWE-41","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["3.1.9"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"3.1.9","date":"2026-10-24","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.096815},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-110095","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110095","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Low","urls":["https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html","https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h"],"description":"fast-uri is a dependency-free RFC 3986 URI parser and serializer for Node.js. In versions before 2.4.8, from 3.0.0 through 3.1.8, and from 4.0.0 through 4.2.2, the normalize() and serialize() functions apply RFC 3986 dot-segment removal to the path of a relative-path reference, even though that algorithm is defined only for the merged target path during resolution, so a leading parent-directory segment can be dropped and a document-relative reference can become root-relative. An application that normalizes an attacker-supplied or user-supplied relative reference and then resolves it, or uses it as a cache, deduplication, or authorization key, can have the reference escape its intended directory and point at a different resource. The issue is fixed in fast-uri 2.4.8, 3.1.9, and 4.2.3, and users should upgrade to one of these versions or later. As a workaround, resolve a relative reference against its absolute base first and normalize the absolute result instead of normalizing the reference beforehand.","cvss":[{"source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":3.7,"exploitabilityScore":2.3,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110095","epss":0.00289,"percentile":0.21831,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-110095","cwe":"CWE-41","source":"ce714d77-add3-4f53-aff5-83d477b104bb","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"fast-uri","version":"3.1.8"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h","versionConstraint":">=3.0.0,<3.1.9 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"3.1.9"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/fast-uri@3.1.8","name":"fast-uri","version":"3.1.8","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["BSD-3-Clause"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/fast-uri@3.1.8","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-46wx-v44x-9hh2","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-46wx-v44x-9hh2","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-46wx-v44x-9hh2","https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/bf16471913b5199212dac33f5d170f94745dd26a","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16"],"description":"Hono: `csrf()` does not check requests sent by hyperlink auditing (`text/ping`)","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":1.7,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126355","epss":0.00176,"percentile":0.0721,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126355","cwe":"CWE-352","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["4.13.16"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"4.13.16","date":"2026-11-13","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.09064},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-126355","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-126355","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/bf16471913b5199212dac33f5d170f94745dd26a","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16","https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-46wx-v44x-9hh2"],"description":"Hono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. Prior to 4.13.16, csrf() limits origin validation to the content types normally sent by HTML forms and therefore does not validate text/ping requests generated by Chromium hyperlink auditing. Chrome and Edge can send a cross-origin credentialed POST without a CORS preflight through an &lt;a ping&gt; action, and the middleware then skips both Origin and Sec-Fetch-Site checks. The fixed request body limits exploitation to state-changing endpoints whose effect is selected by the path or query string and does not depend on submitted body data. The user's cookie must accompany the request, which generally requires a same-site origin or a cookie configured with SameSite=None, and Firefox does not send hyperlink-auditing pings by default. This issue is fixed in version 4.13.16.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":5.3,"exploitabilityScore":1.7,"impactScore":3.6},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126355","epss":0.00176,"percentile":0.0721,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126355","cwe":"CWE-352","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"hono","version":"4.13.13"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-46wx-v44x-9hh2","versionConstraint":"<4.13.16 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"4.13.16"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","name":"hono","version":"4.13.13","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-3gg2-335m-rxc6","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3gg2-335m-rxc6","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Low","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-3gg2-335m-rxc6","https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/15bbd96ad1b62a0b189db4fd8dc7bf8ef280c513","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16"],"description":"Hono: `css` helper does not escape a closing tag split between the template and an interpolated value, allowing HTML injection","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:N/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":3.4,"exploitabilityScore":1.7,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126359","epss":0.00262,"percentile":0.18101,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126359","cwe":"CWE-79","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["4.13.16"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"4.13.16","date":"2026-11-13","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.08383999999999998},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-126359","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-126359","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Low","urls":["https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/15bbd96ad1b62a0b189db4fd8dc7bf8ef280c513","https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases/tag/v4.13.16","https://github.com/honojs/hono/security/advisories/GHSA-3gg2-335m-rxc6"],"description":"Hono is a Web application framework that provides support for any JavaScript runtime. From 3.12.0 until 4.13.16, the css helper in hono/css escapes interpolated string values separately and therefore fails to neutralize a closing style tag when &lt; ends the template text or a preceding value and / begins the next attacker-controlled value. During server-side rendering, the combined output can close the &lt;Style /&gt; element early and cause the remainder of the interpolated value to be interpreted as HTML. Applications that place an untrusted string immediately after &lt; in a css template, including adjacent untrusted interpolations, can expose viewers to attacker-controlled HTML or script and information accessible to that page. Other uses of the css helper are not affected. This issue is fixed in version 4.13.16.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:N/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":3.4,"exploitabilityScore":1.7,"impactScore":1.5},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126359","epss":0.00262,"percentile":0.18101,"date":"2026-11-22"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-126359","cwe":"CWE-79","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"hono","version":"4.13.13"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-3gg2-335m-rxc6","versionConstraint":">=3.12.0,<=4.13.15 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"4.13.16"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","name":"hono","version":"4.13.13","type":"npm","locations":null,"language":"javascript","licenses":["MIT"],"cpes":[],"purl":"pkg:npm/hono@4.13.13","upstreams":[]}}],"source":{"type":"sbom-file","target":"/Users/rithvikrajesh/Projects/Dummies/Software-Supply-Chain-Guardian_Team-31/data/scans/vignes-vm__udhaar-mcp__20261123-114849/sbom/bom.json"},"distro":{"name":"","version":"","idLike":null},"descriptor":{"name":"grype","version":"0.122.1","configuration":{"output":["json"],"file":"